  "limits": [
    "Offline backup and restoration are bounded whole-namespace/file inventories, additionally limited by native transaction bytes/lifetime; this is not FoundationDB large online backup.",
    "Versioned Node/V8 backup is not an automatic cross-runtime/catalog or historical Rust format migration.",
    "One owned local FoundationDB process/coordinator does not certify replication, disk/power loss or server-failure recovery.",
    "SIGKILL and committed response loss are verified; native commit-ack fault injection and actual power loss are not.",
    "Provider restore fencing is verified against independent durable fake Resend/Brevo ledgers. Live email/SMS, retention windows and remote protocol acceptance remain unverified; unsupported restored work isolates.",
    "Custody and deployment files stay outside releases/backups; operator must retain old encryption keys and coordinate separate activation processes.",
    "Privileged raw handles can bypass runtime admission; every writer must obey the pause. No unbounded hostile filesystem race claim.",
    "Locked extracted source installation and repeated same-host npm archive bytes are verified. Arbitrary native build identity and arbitrary host dependency-tree resolution are not certified.",
    "No remote host/TLS deployment was performed; a concrete operator target is required.",
    "128-row/40-step workload is a small local fixture. Native client key/value bytes exclude network framing, disk amplification and replication; RSS is process lifetime high-water, not per-operation allocation.",
    "Online catalog migration/catch-up, durable cursors, multi-host writes, larger capacity, recurrence, live feeds, frontend and full accounting/domain suites remain separate obligations."
  ],
